'''''Lepidocystis''''' is the type genus and first-discovered member of the family [[Lepidocystidae]],<ref>TREATISE</ref> the most [[basal]] known group of [[Blastozoa]]ns.<ref>{{harvnb|Sprinkle|1973}}</ref>

==Morphology==

''Lepidocystis'' is a stalked, sessile echinoderm with imbricate plates on the stalk and sides of the theca, and tesselate plates on the sharply delineated oral surface.  The oral surface, which is not always the widest part of the theca, contains five recumbent ambulacra, with brachioles arising along them on alternating sides.

